    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d864">

                <pb facs="1105" n="1003" xml:id="pg1003"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.003/132: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-17T15:00:00+00:00">January 17, 1935—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 17—1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. Department’s 4, January 16, 6 p.m. Is point (2) Blake’s proposal regarding
                    Kettani claim satisfactory? May we, without mentioning capitulations, concede,
                    if necessary, that after settlement of claims and recognition any point raised
                    by Spanish Government will, of course, have to be considered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
